custom-notification-daemon for Debian/Ubuntu
===========================================

If another notification daemon is already running, disable it first:

  systemctl --user disable --now dunst.service 2>/dev/null || true
  systemctl --user disable --now mako.service 2>/dev/null || true

For Sway sessions, start this daemon directly from Sway config.
Add this line to your sway config:

  exec_always --no-startup-id custom-notification-daemon run
